    [Test] Migrate GLM-5.3-Flash A3 PD nightly to V2 PCP (#20108)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Run the existing A3 `GLM-5.3-Flash-W8A8-130k-PD` nightly with Model
    Runner V2 and PCP. Replace Prefill DP2/TP8 with DP2/TP1/PCP8, disable
    legacy DSA CP, and update the Prefill TP metadata in both
    MooncakeConnectorV2 configurations. Decode remains DP8/TP2. Both nodes
    continue using 16 NPUs each.
    
    Preserve int8 KV, MTP5, memory settings, graph/compilation settings,
    model, and existing benchmark workloads. Performance uses
    `vllm-ascend/GSM8K_prefix100_in16384_bs500_GLM5_3_flash_w8a8`: warmup 4
    requests/concurrency 1, formal 512 requests/concurrency 128, output
    1024. Accuracy remains AIME2025. Update the internal test name from V1
    to V2 while preserving the nightly trigger name.
    
    This isolates the Flash configuration migration from #19500. Only the
    existing Flash YAML changes; no nightly registry or shared workflow
    changes are needed. The branch is based on main including Flash PCP
    support #18511.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This modifies an existing nightly configuration only.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Loaded YAML with the repository ExternalDPConfigLoader, resolved all
    10 ranks and rendered all server commands with
    RankResolver/ServerCommandBuilder. Confirmed V2 on every rank, P
    DP2/TP1/PCP8, D DP8/TP2 and 16 NPUs per node.
    - Validated embedded JSON, disabled Prefill DSA CP and consistent
    Mooncake P/D metadata. Verified the extracted configuration exactly
    matches the Flash configuration from #19500 and benchmark workloads are
    unchanged from main apart from the calibrated formal performance
    baseline and threshold.
    - `git diff --check`: passed.
    - `bash format.sh ci`: attempted; blocked by local pre-commit being
    unavailable.
    - Three completed V2/PCP runs validated the same
    512-request/concurrency-128 workload:
    [40667247430](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40667247430)
    at 4306.6237 token/s,
    [40675293823](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40675293823)
    at 4317.1039 token/s, and
    [40800575989](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40800575989)
    at 4248.503 token/s. Each had 512/512 successful performance requests
    and AIME2025 28/30. Set the formal baseline to the minimum, 4248.503
    token/s, with threshold 0.95 (4036.07785 token/s). Warmup and accuracy
    settings are unchanged.
    - Baseline update: YAML parsing and semantic comparison confirmed only
    the formal baseline/threshold changed; git diff --check passed. The
    required format check remains blocked by missing local pre-commit. No
    new nightly was triggered for this metadata update.
    
    Use the existing case command for hardware validation: `/nightly
    GLM-5.3-Flash-W8A8-130k-PD`.
    
    No additional test files were added: the existing nightly
    accuracy/performance workload covers this configuration.
    
    Latest main synchronization (2026-10-29): merged upstream
    `2d6654fbd170d110eec9c6cb30c55751045c4d8d` into
    `375592cff9795370abcd73ff37d66553246ef4d8` without conflicts. Confirmed
    the Flash configuration, 10 resolved ranks, V2/PCP8, Mooncake metadata,
    and calibrated baseline 4248.503 / threshold 0.95 are preserved. PR diff
    whitespace check passed; full format check remains blocked by missing
    local pre-commit. Merge-only whitespace warnings belong to upstream
    files. A fresh nightly is being requested below to validate the updated
    dependencies.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
